{
  "_readme": "Vectors for WISHMAIL_SPEC_v0_5.md §7.2 — the AAD and the envelope identifier. T-P1-4: every class recomputes `bytes` and `id` from `header` exactly. The key names are §7.2’s six and no others (D-127); `bytes` is their RFC 8785 canonical JSON, which sorts them l, lane, nc, p, rp, v whatever order they are written in; `id` is SHA-256 over `bytes`, lowercase hex. `rebuild` is §5.6’s other direction: a reader with chunk 0’s `hdr` and the topic the chunk arrived on rebuilds the same bytes and so binds the header to the `id` every chunk carries. Lane and proof identifiers here are well-formed and synthetic — the AAD is a function of its six fields and of nothing on any ledger. Frozen; regenerating is a decision, not a chore.",
